.SH "[0\&.50\&.00] - 03\&.07\&.2026 -> Lacking"
.PP
.SS "Major Documentation Milestone"
A significant version jump was made intentionally\&. 
.br
 With this release, the entire public API of \fBSystemEx\fP — including the mathematical canvas system, layer model, blend modes, hash engines, and all related interfaces — has been fully documented and formalized\&.

.PP
This marks the completion of approximately half of the planned major‑release scope\&. The version number reflects this structural maturity rather than incremental feature changes\&.
.SS "Added"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Full XML documentation for all canvas interfaces (\fRICanvas\fP, \fRISubCanvas\fP, \fRICanvasList\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Complete documentation for all hash engines (Groestl, Adler, etc\&.)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Formalized mathematical layer model and blend mode semantics
.IP "\(bu" 2
Unified terminology across the entire \fBSystemEx\fP framework
.PP
.SS "Changed"
.IP "\(bu" 2
API surface stabilized and prepared for 1\&.0
.IP "\(bu" 2
Internal consistency improvements across all canvas and hash components
.PP
.SS "Notes"
The jump from \fR0\&.12\&.04\fP to \fR0\&.50\&.00\fP is intentional and represents reaching the halfway point toward the 1\&.0 major release\&.
.SS "Codename Update: Ignoring → Lacking"
The codename for the 0\&.x development cycle has been updated from \fBIgnoring\fP to \fBLacking\fP\&.

.PP
All \fBSystemEx\fP development codenames follow the theme of “Missing”, reflecting the project’s purpose of providing features, structures, and utilities that are missing in the \&.NET ecosystem\&.

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBIgnoring\fP represented the early phase where documentation, structure, and formal API descriptions were intentionally ignored while core functionality was being built\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBLacking\fP represents the next phase: the system is functionally complete, but still lacking documentation, clarity, and formal definitions\&.
.PP

.PP
With version \fB0\&.50\&.00\fP, the documentation milestone has been reached, marking the end of the “Lacking” phase\&. All subsequent 0\&.50\&.x versions will continue under this codename until the remaining missing structural components are completed\&.

.PP
