.SS "Added"
\fRSystem\&.FlexSpan<T>\fP — a unified view type for array‑based memory\&.** 
.br
 FlexSpan implements three indexing modes: 
.br
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRSystemSpan\fP (forward indexing) 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRReverseSpan\fP (reverse indexing) 
.br

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRRingSpan\fP (circular indexing)
.PP

.PP
FlexSpan operates directly on \fBraw \fRT[]\fP buffers\fP without allocation and provides ref‑return access to elements\&. 
.br
 It is now integrated across all \fB\fBSystemEx\&.Collections\fP\fP types that use array‑backed storage (Stack, Array, FixedArray, Cache, StrippedCache)\&. 
.br

.PP
Map‑based collections are not yet supported because they use \fRList<T>\fP internally\&. 
.br
 A dedicated \fBFlexListSpan\fP type will be added later to enable FlexSpan‑style views over list‑backed containers\&.

.PP
